     "text": "{\"attack_techniques\": [{\"id\": \"T1110\", \"name\": \"Brute Force\", \"tactics\": [\"Credential Access\"], \"why_relevant\": \"The alert shows 3 failed authentication attempts with invalid credentials on user rthompson, indicating a potential brute force attack against the account.\"}, {\"id\": \"T1078\", \"name\": \"Valid Accounts\", \"tactics\": [\"Stealth\", \"Persistence\", \"Privilege Escalation\", \"Initial Access\"], \"why_relevant\": \"The failed authentication attempts target the legitimate account rthompson, suggesting the attacker is attempting to compromise valid credentials for unauthorized access.\"}, {\"id\": \"T1021.006\", \"name\": \"Windows Remote Management\", \"tactics\": [\"Lateral Movement\"], \"why_relevant\": \"The Kerberos authentication failures indicate potential attempts to gain remote access through Windows authentication mechanisms after credential compromise.\"}], \"identity_signals\": {\"impossible_travel\": false, \"mfa_fatigue\": false, \"privilege_escalation\": false, \"dormant_account_reactivation\": false, \"notes\": \"No identity signals detected. No affected users identified. No anomalous sign-in patterns observed.\"}, \"key_findings\": \"Three failed Kerberos authentication attempts were observed against the legitimate user account rthompson from source IP 198.51.100.88, consistent with a credential brute force attack. The authentication system successfully denied all attempts due to invalid credentials, preventing unauthorized access. No identity signals indicate compromise or lateral movement success.\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"severity_rationale\": \"This is an attack attempt from an external source (198.51.100.88) that the authentication control stopped at the perimeter\u2014all three attempts failed and were denied by the Kerberos mechanism. There is no evidence that any internal account or host was compromised, no successful authentication, and no indication that the attacker gained access to resources or data. The attack was blocked before reaching internal systems.\", \"confidence\": 0.75, \"recommended_response\": \"Monitor the rthompson account and source IP 198.51.100.88 for further brute force attempts. Consider implementing rate limiting or account lockout policies if not already in place. If brute force activity persists from this or other IPs targeting the same account, escalate to medium or high severity and implement additional controls such as IP blocking or enhanced MFA enforcement for the affected account.\", \"rounds_used\": 0}",
     "type": "text"
    }
