   "container": null,
   "content": [
    {
     "citations": null,
     "text": "{\"completeness\": 0.85, \"citation_quality\": 0.65, \"severity_defensibility\": 0.75, \"overall_pass\": true, \"feedback\": \"The investigation demonstrates solid foundational analysis with clear reasoning about the blocked attack and appropriate severity calibration. However, citation quality needs improvement: T1110 (Brute Force) is well-justified by the three failed attempts, but T1078 (Valid Accounts) and especially T1021.006 (WinRM) are poorly connected to the evidence\u2014there is no indication the attacker possessed valid credentials or attempted remote management. Remove or replace these misaligned techniques. Additionally, the identity_signals section shows all zeroes with empty evidence fields, which seems incomplete; explicitly state why each signal (impossible travel, MFA fatigue, etc.) was ruled out or note if data was unavailable. Finally, while the recommendation to monitor is sound, consider adding more specific thresholds (e.g., 'escalate if 5+ attempts within 30 minutes' or 'block IP after X failed attempts') to make the guidance more actionable. These refinements will strengthen the triage for future similar alerts.\"}",
     "type": "text"
    }
